From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:44:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sc8547_svooc: hold VBUS against both readings
 of the battery

The running check held the bus between twice the gauge's voltage less
100 mV and twice it plus 700 mV. Under 9 A the gauge reads the cell
plus the drop to it, some 100 mV above the main pump's own sense at its
battery pins, and when the adapter steps its output the current falls
within a frame while the gauge's reading follows later. At the second
timed step of the factory adapter on the OnePlus Pad 4 (flight D1,
+16:00, 67 %) the bus fell to 8.415 V, the pump read 4.168 V and the
gauge still 4.270 V: the floor, 8.44 V, ended the session (-ERANGE), the
adapter dropped to 5 V and re-attached, and each session the driver
then started at 3 A ended the same way within a second, the gauge
sitting above the pump's sense while it settled, four times over.

Hold the bus against both readings: the floor follows the lower, the
ceiling the higher, so a step of the adapter or a gauge that lags does
not end a session, while a bus below twice the lowest reading of the
battery or above twice the highest plus 700 mV still does. KUnit pins
the end of flight D1 on both sides of the new floor and the ceiling.

Before the pumps take the input, when both readings are unloaded,
require them to agree within 150 mV, else refuse the adapter (-EIO): a
pump whose battery sense is loose must not be the one the adapter
regulates against.

Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.c      |   11 +++++---
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c |   30 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c              |   14 +++++++++-
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.c
index 2be337ca4412..255e062c2353 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.c
@@ -279,9 +279,11 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sc8547_direct_regulate_target_ua);
  * @disagree: how many samples in a row the pumps' VBUS disagreed, kept by
  *	the caller and updated here
  *
- * VBUS is held against the gauge's voltage, not against the pump's own
- * sense of the battery. A second pump that stops is the caller's to see off,
- * not a fault of the session.
+ * VBUS is held against both readings of the battery: the gauge's, which
+ * carries the drop to the cell under current and lags a step of the
+ * adapter, and the main pump's own sense; the window's floor follows the
+ * lower reading and its ceiling the higher. A second pump that stops is the
+ * caller's to see off, not a fault of the session.
  *
  * Return: 0, -EIO when the main pump does not switch, -ERANGE when a
  * voltage, a current or the power left its window.
@@ -296,7 +298,8 @@ int sc8547_direct_running_ok(const struct sc8547_sample *main,
 
 	if (!main->switching)
 		return -EIO;
-	if (main->vbus_uv < 2 * vbat_uv - 100000 || main->vbus_uv > 2 * vbat_uv + 700000)
+	if (main->vbus_uv < 2 * min(vbat_uv, main->vbat_uv) - 100000 ||
+	    main->vbus_uv > 2 * max(vbat_uv, main->vbat_uv) + 700000)
 		return -ERANGE;
 	/*
 	 * Each pump within its own maximum; the main alone within it while
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
index 30ab6f424962..512e01dd4069 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
@@ -471,19 +471,43 @@ static void sc8547_direct_test_running_window(struct kunit *test)
 						       &disagree), -ERANGE);
 
 	/*
-	 * The window is referenced to the gauge, not to the pump's sense of the
-	 * battery: a low pump reading does not shift it, a low gauge reading does.
+	 * The window follows both readings of the battery: its floor the lower,
+	 * its ceiling the higher. A bus at 8.0 V passes a pump reading of 3.0 V
+	 * against a gauge at 4.0 V (floor 5.9 V) and the other way round
+	 * (ceiling 8.7 V); a gauge at 3.65 V and a pump at 4.0 V too.
 	 */
 	m = main_running;
 	m.vbat_uv = 3000000;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 4000000, 6200000, false, false,
 						       &disagree), 0);
 	m.vbat_uv = 4000000;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 3000000, 6200000, false, false,
+						       &disagree), 0);
+	m.vbus_uv = 8700001;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 3000000, 6200000, false, false,
 						       &disagree), -ERANGE);
-	m.vbat_uv = 4000000;
+	m.vbus_uv = 8000000;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 3650000, 6200000, false, false,
 						       &disagree), 0);
+	/*
+	 * The end of flight D1: the adapter stepped its output, the bus fell to
+	 * 8.415 V, the pump read 4.168 V and the gauge, still carrying the drop
+	 * of the current just removed, 4.270 V. The old floor, 8.44 V, ended the
+	 * session; the floor on the lower reading, 8.236 V, does not.
+	 */
+	m.vbat_uv = 4168000;
+	m.vbus_uv = 8415000;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 4270000, 6200000, false, false,
+						       &disagree), 0);
+	m.vbus_uv = 8235999;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 4270000, 6200000, false, false,
+						       &disagree), -ERANGE);
+	m.vbus_uv = 9240000;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 4270000, 6200000, false, false,
+						       &disagree), 0);
+	m.vbus_uv = 9240001;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_running_ok(&m, &s, 4270000, 6200000, false, false,
+						       &disagree), -ERANGE);
 
 	/* A main pump that is not switching fails before anything else. */
 	m = main_running;
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
index 53cbc4c57828..66ff1556adb1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@
  * this many frames (some 400 ms at the adapter's cadence).
  */
 #define SVOOC_SECOND_FEED_FRAMES	8
+/*
+ * Before the pumps take the input, the gauge's and the main pump's readings
+ * of the battery, both unloaded then, must agree to this.
+ */
+#define SVOOC_SENSE_AGREE_UV	150000
 
 #define SVOOC_TICK_MS		50
 #define SVOOC_BUCK_TICK_MS	20
@@ -444,8 +449,13 @@ static int svooc_power_command(struct sc8547_svooc *sv,
 		if (sv->state != SVOOC_GRANTED && sv->state != SVOOC_STARTING &&
 		    sv->state != SVOOC_RUNNING)
 			return -EPROTO;
-		/* Read after the last reply, as the factory driver does. */
-		/* Against the pump's own battery sense, as the factory driver. */
+		/*
+		 * Read after the last reply, against the pump's own battery
+		 * sense, as the factory driver does; a pump whose sense and the
+		 * gauge disagree does not get the input.
+		 */
+		if (abs(sv->sample[0].vbat_uv - sv->bat.uv) > SVOOC_SENSE_AGREE_UV)
+			return -EIO;
 		*payload = oplus_svooc_vbus(sv->sample[0].vbus_uv, sv->sample[0].vbat_uv);
 		/* The pump switches on before the adapter hears "normal". */
 		if (*payload == OPLUS_SVOOC_VBUS_NORMAL && sv->state == SVOOC_GRANTED) {
